<title>BRAZIL: Sao Paulo Aug unemployment at 15.5 pct - Dieese.</title>
<headline>Sao Paulo Aug unemployment at 15.5 pct - Dieese.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1996-09-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The unemployment rate in Sao Paulo city fell for the second consecutive month to 15.5 percent in August, down from 15.7 percent in July, the Labor Union Statistics Institute (Dieese) reported.</p>
<p>The number of unemployed workers fell to 1.322 million in August, down from 1.335 million in July, it said.</p>
<p>August figures, however, rose against the same month last year, when the share of unemployed workers was 12.9 percent of the workforce, or 1.052 million workers, it added.</p>
<p>-- Romina Nicaretta, Sao Paulo newsroom, 55-11-2324411</p>
